  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oven to 425 F. Line a large rimmed sheet pan with parchment paper.",
    "Toss the sweet potatoes with 2 tbsp olive oil, 1/2 tsp salt, and 1/8 tsp pepper on the pan. Spread them out and roast for 10 minutes.",
    "Mix the Dijon, garlic, thyme, 1 tbsp olive oil, 1 tsp salt, and 1/2 tsp pepper in a small bowl. Pat the pork dry and rub the mixture all over it.",
    "Toss the broccoli with 1 tbsp olive oil, 1/4 tsp salt, and 1/8 tsp pepper in the bowl you used for the potatoes.",
    "Pull the pan from the oven. Push the potatoes to the sides and set the pork in the center. Scatter the broccoli around the pork.",
    "Roast for 18 to 22 minutes, until the pork reads 145 F in the thickest part and the potatoes are tender and browned at the edges.",
    "Rest the pork on a cutting board for 5 minutes. Slice it into 1/2 inch rounds and serve with the vegetables."
  ],
